WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.390
- Athletes do many of the
same things when they retire.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.910
Gronk and his former
teammate, Julian Edelman,

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.920
recently had some fun with that.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.270
So let's see it.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.620
- We're retired athletes.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.120
We're gonna get jobs on TV.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.080
- We're retired athletes.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.250
We're gonna tease a comeback.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.570
- We're retired athletes.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.430
We're gonna watch our old highlights.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.720
- We're retired athletes.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.255
We're gonna start a podcast.

00:00:20.255 --> 00:00:21.893
(audience cheering)

00:00:21.893 --> 00:00:23.580
- This should have been an "SNL" skit.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.413
It's so funny.

00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:25.600
They should do that
with musicians as well.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.030
- We're retired athletes.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.272
We go on "The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:00:28.272 --> 00:00:29.619
- There you go.
(audience cheering)

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:31.093
Good times, good times.

00:00:31.093 --> 00:00:32.573
So wait, whose idea is that?

00:00:32.573 --> 00:00:34.350
Are you into social media?

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.610
- A little bit.
- Okay.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.720
- Yeah, social media's cool.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.430
You gotta use it for the right reasons.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.990
But I was at Julian Edelman's house,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.330
he has a great podcast
called "Names with Games."

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.010
- Yeah.
- And we just did his podcast

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.659
and he has his whole
social media team there.

00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:47.697
And then they showed me
this new trend on TikTok

00:00:47.697 --> 00:00:49.110
and that was the new trend.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.250
And they were like, "We're gonna do it

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.590
as retired athletes," and
it was such a great idea

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.030
and it came out so good.
- So funny.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.230
I know, I was telling you on the break,

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:56.550
I was like, "That should
have been on 'SNL.'"

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.500
That would've been a really funny skit.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.940
Yeah, so you have a new partner

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.800
for "Big Game Parties." Who is it?

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:02.910
- Yes, I actually do.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.310
And Julian Edelman is
now a part of it as well.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.410
And this is my second year
teaming up with Bounty.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.850
And that's why I'm in my green suit

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.160
because I am the Bounty Man.
- Yeah.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.160
- Yes, there's no doubt

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.157
about that.
- And green is a great color.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:15.840
- And I'm from Buffalo,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.210
so I know a thing or two about Buffalo.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.320
Wings as well.
- Yeah, I love wings.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.120
- You gotta always have
blue cheese on the side

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.140
when you're from Buffalo.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.720
And you can't have football without wings.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.285
And you can't have wings without Bounty.

00:01:27.285 --> 00:01:28.170
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.940
- I can't have-
- Because it gets saucy,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:30.773
it gets messy.

00:01:30.773 --> 00:01:31.890
- [Both] The quicker picker upper.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.240
- I just (smacks lips)...
- I got you.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.410
- Cleans you right up.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.907
- Quicker picker upper, I remember that.

00:01:35.907 --> 00:01:38.070
No, I agree with all of that.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.990
Except not the blue cheese.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.174
I have to have ranch.

00:01:41.174 --> 00:01:44.340
- Yeah!
(audience cheers)

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.900
- When you're from Buffalo...
- I'm Texan.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.200
- When you're from Buffalo,
you use blue cheese only.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.060
- When you're Texan you put ranch

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.040
or ketchup on everything.
- Yes.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.300
But when you're from Buffalo,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.950
you gotta have the buffalo blue cheese.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.300
But if you're outside of Buffalo...

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.860
- Okay.
- I won't make the argument.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.120
Yes, you can have ranch

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.246
'cause the buffalo blue cheese is the only

00:02:02.246 --> 00:02:04.680
legit blue cheese out there.
- I like blue cheese.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.610
I like blue cheese.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.690
But there's something (smacks lips)

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.520
about ranch that I really love.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.360
- Nope, blue cheese.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:10.292
- Really, I just want the ranch.

00:02:10.292 --> 00:02:11.490
- You gotta go with buffalo.
- And I just want it.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.816
I need something, the
vessel for it to get there.

00:02:13.816 --> 00:02:15.090
- Wait until you have
the buffalo blue cheese.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.220
- Okay, I have had buffalo blue.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.660
I like it, I like it.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.828
And maybe when I'm in Buffalo-
- Where'd you go?

00:02:19.828 --> 00:02:21.090
- I'll do that.
- Yes, when you're in buffalo.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.797
- Everywhere else I say, "No."

